# The CI changes this branch could not carry.
#
# Why this is a file and not a commit: the GitHub connection this work ran
# through is a GitHub App installation without the `workflows` permission, and
# GitHub refuses any push whose net effect updates a file under
# `.github/workflows/`. Every attempt was rejected with
#
#   refusing to allow a GitHub App to create or update workflow
#   `.github/workflows/build.yml` without `workflows` permission
#
# The rule is evaluated on the diff, not on the commits: a branch whose tip has
# the workflows as they are on `master` pushes fine even when earlier commits in
# it edited them (that is what the push that created this branch did). So the
# workflow edits are kept here, in the form Git would have applied them.
#
# What it contains, cut against master at fb97d48:
#   build.yml       - drops the release step that ran check-no-test-pro.mjs
#   checks.yml      - adds the site build and its SEO gate, ESLint, Prettier,
#                     the model suites, the coverage ratchet and the isolated
#                     native policy tests; drops the check-no-test-pro step
#   deploy-site.yml - rebuilds the site when the shared modules it imports from
#                     src/ change
#
# To apply, from the repository root, with the workflow permission in place:
#
#   git apply docs/ci-workflow-changes.patch
#   git add .github/workflows && git commit -m "CI: the gates npm run check runs"
#
# Until then, two steps on master still call scripts/check-no-test-pro.mjs,
# which this branch retires; they will fail if the workflow runs. Deleting them
# is the first hunk above.
diff --git a/.github/workflows/build.yml b/.github/workflows/build.yml
index 038d776..0908d39 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/build.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/build.yml
@@ -40,7 +40,3 @@ jobs:
       - name: Build without distributing verification artifacts
         shell: bash
         run: npm run tauri build -- --config '{"bundle":{"createUpdaterArtifacts":false}}'
-
-      # The Pro unlock of VM test builds must never be in a release.
-      - name: Refuse release binaries built with the test unlock
-        run: node scripts/check-no-test-pro.mjs --binary src-tauri/target/release
